## Settings Page Sections

Settings partial (`checklistdek-settings-page.php`) uses Settings API form with `.checklistdek-settings-nav` client-side tabs (`data-checklistdek-settings-tab` / `data-checklistdek-settings-panel`: `platform-security`, `panel-exclude`, `webhooks-email`, `access-roles`; `initSettingsTabs()` in admin JS syncs `?tab=`). Single form submit saves all sections. `onboarding_dismissed` is REST-only (`POST /onboarding/dismiss|reset`) — not a Settings form checkbox (saving settings does not reset or toggle it; sanitizer preserves the key when passed in `$input`). Same pattern for `wp_umbrella_api_token_enc` (Integrations admin-ajax only) and `custom_site_groups` (Sites REST groups).

**Platform & Security** tab:
- **Platform** — `enabled`, `drift_verification_enabled`
- **Credential Vault Security** — `encrypt_credentials` toggle

**Panel layout & Exclude** tab:
- **Exclude Options** — `#checklistdek-exclude-options` textarea (`exclude_options`; one REST field or legacy option name per line via `CHECKLISTDEK_Settings::format_exclude_options_textarea()`; defaults `url`, `email`, `wp_environment_type`; aliases via `get_exclude_option_aliases()` / `normalize_exclude_option()`; common-field hints list via `get_exclude_option_labels()` → `.checklistdek-settings-exclude-common-fields`)
- **Client Checklist Panel** — `#checklistdek-panel-layout` select (`client_panel_layout`; options from `CHECKLISTDEK_Licensing::get_panel_layouts_for_plan()` — Community subset of `CHECKLISTDEK_Settings::get_client_panel_layouts()`; saved value sanitized via `CHECKLISTDEK_Licensing::sanitize_panel_layout()`; snapshots use `get_effective_panel_layout()`); live preview via `#checklistdek-panel-layout-preview` (`initPanelLayoutPreview()`); `#checklistdek-client-panel-title` text input (`client_panel_title`, default `Agency Checklist`, max 80 chars — syncs on next push or panel refresh)

**Webhooks & Email** tab:
- **Notification Channels** — Slack/Teams/Discord webhooks + event checkboxes (`CHECKLISTDEK_Settings::get_notification_events()`)
- **Email Notifications** — `.checklistdek-settings-email-events` event checkboxes (`CHECKLISTDEK_Settings::get_email_notification_events()` → `email_notification_events[]`); `#checklistdek-email-notification-address` text input (`email_notification_address`, comma-separated; placeholder defaults to site admin email)

**Access & Roles** tab:
- **Agency Role Guardrails** — preset cards (`get_agency_role_presets()`) + role-permission matrix (`role_permissions`)
- **Onboarding** — `#checklistdek-show-onboarding` button; requires shared onboarding + template-picker modal partials below the form

Section headings use `.checklistdek-card-heading-row--info-first` with `.checklistdek-field-info.checklistdek-has-tooltip` info buttons (`data-tooltip` from `$section_tooltips` in the Settings partial; same pattern on Integrations).

Telemetry sync rules are managed on the Integrations page (REST), not the Settings form.

Onboarding REST handlers in `CHECKLISTDEK_REST_API`:
- `POST /onboarding/dismiss` → `dismiss_onboarding()` (`can_view_dashboard`) — sets `onboarding_dismissed` to `true`
- `POST /onboarding/reset` → `reset_onboarding()` (`can_manage_settings`) — sets `onboarding_dismissed` to `false` for Settings preview

Settings REST handlers in `CHECKLISTDEK_REST_API`:
- `POST /settings/client-panel-title` → `update_client_panel_title()` (`can_edit_checklists`) — `CHECKLISTDEK_Settings::save_client_panel_title()`; builder auto-save

Billing REST handlers in `CHECKLISTDEK_REST_API` (registered only when `checklistdek_includes_pro_package()`):
- `GET /billing/summary` → `get_billing_summary()` (`can_view_dashboard`) — `CHECKLISTDEK_Licensing::get_summary()`
- `POST /billing/plan` → `update_billing_plan()` (`can_manage_settings`) — `{ plan }` → `set_plan()`; returns updated summary

Dashboard / audit REST handlers in `CHECKLISTDEK_REST_API`:
- `GET /logs/run/{run_id}/steps` → `get_log_run_steps()` (`can_view_dashboard`) — `CHECKLISTDEK_Audit_Log::get_run_steps_timeline()`
- `GET /logs/{id}` → `get_log_entry()` — optional `details_only=1` returns lean `{ id, details, has_details }` via `get_decoded_details()` (Activity Logs **View raw data**)

Client panel REST handlers in `CHECKLISTDEK_REST_API`:
- `GET /panel/bootstrap` → `get_panel_bootstrap()` (`can_manage_sites`) — returns mu-plugin loader file for manual download
- `GET /sites/groups` → `get_site_groups()` (`can_manage_sites`) — `CHECKLISTDEK_Settings::get_site_group_catalog()`
- `POST /sites/groups` → `create_site_group()` (`can_manage_sites`) — `{ label }` → `add_custom_site_group()`; returns `{ group, groups }`
- `POST /sites/{id}/panel/install` → `install_site_panel()` (`can_manage_sites`) — retries `CHECKLISTDEK_Mu_Plugin_Installer::ensure_installed()` (Sites modal **Retry panel install**)
- `GET /sites/{id}/runs` → `get_site_runs()` (`can_manage_sites`) — checklist run history (admin UI uses admin-ajax `checklistdek_get_site_runs`; REST retained for programmatic access) via `list_for_site_history()` (optional `status`, `limit` default 25 max 200, `offset`; returns `{ runs, has_more, offset, limit }`)
- `POST /runs/{id}/archive` → `archive_run()` (`can_manage_sites`) — soft-hide run from default history (`CHECKLISTDEK_Run_Repository::archive()`)
- `DELETE /runs/{id}` → `delete_run()` (`can_manage_sites`) — permanently delete run and step rows (`CHECKLISTDEK_Run_Repository::delete()`)
- `GET|POST|DELETE /sites/{id}/capture` → `get_site_capture()` / `update_site_capture()` / `clear_site_capture()` (`can_edit_checklists`) — proxies to `CHECKLISTDEK_Auto_Capture`
- `POST /runs` → optional `push_to_client` (bool, default `true`); when set, calls `CHECKLISTDEK_Client_Push::push_run()` after start
- `POST /runs/{id}/steps/{step}/uncomplete` → `uncomplete_manual_step()` (`can_execute`) — `CHECKLISTDEK_Step_Executor::mark_manual_incomplete()` then `sync_run()`
- `POST /runs/{id}/push-client` → `push_run_to_client()` (`can_execute`) — `push_run( $id, false, true )` snapshot re-push + bundle sync, no auto-advance (Automation **Refresh Client Panel**)
- `POST /client-runs/{id}/steps/{step}/complete` → `client_complete_step()` (`can_client_token_access_run`) — `complete_client_step( …, true )` (`$skip_client_sync`); returns `snapshot`
- `POST /client-runs/{id}/steps/{step}/uncomplete` → `client_uncomplete_step()` (`can_client_token_access_run`) — `uncomplete_client_step( …, true )`; returns `snapshot`
- `POST /client-runs/{id}/steps/{step}/notes` → `client_add_step_note()` (`can_client_token_access_run`) — `add_client_step_note( …, true )`; returns `snapshot`
- Run advance handlers (`/next`, `/auto`, manual complete/uncomplete) call `CHECKLISTDEK_Client_Push::sync_run()` when panel is available

Remote mu-plugin REST (`mu-plugin/checklistdek-client/class-rest-api.php`, namespace `checklistdek/v1`):
- `GET /client/info` — public panel probe
- `POST /client/install` — hub pushes whitelisted bundle files (`can_hub_manage` via Application Password)
- `GET|POST|DELETE /client/run` — active run snapshot CRUD
- `POST /client/run/dismiss` — clear completed checklist from client panel (local snapshot only)
- `POST /client/run/steps/{step}/complete` — client user completes step; callbacks to hub with run token
- `POST /client/run/steps/{step}/uncomplete` — client user reverts completed manual step; callbacks to hub with run token
- `POST /client/run/steps/{step}/notes` — saves note locally via `CHECKLISTDEK_Client_Run_Store::add_step_note()`, then syncs to hub (`hub_synced` flag); notes require non-empty text; optional `attachment_id`/`attachment_url` from remote `wp.media`
- `GET|POST|DELETE /client/capture` — auto-capture session status, start/stop, clear captured steps

Client `CHECKLISTDEK_Client_Run_Store::save()` merges local notes with incoming hub snapshots via `merge_step_notes()`; `patch_from_hub_run()` preserves local note data on partial hub responses. Client panel assets in `mu-plugin/checklistdek-client/{css,js}/` — prefix selectors with `.checklistdek-client-*`; localize `checklistdekClient` global.

When editing the client panel bundle, keep hub installer paths (`CHECKLISTDEK_Mu_Plugin_Installer::BUNDLE_DIR`) and remote loader (`mu-plugin/checklistdek-client.php`) in sync.

Integration REST handlers in `CHECKLISTDEK_REST_API`:
- `GET /integrations` → `get_integrations()` (`can_manage_settings`) — `CHECKLISTDEK_Integrations::get_statuses()`
- `POST /integrations/{slug}/sync` → `sync_integration()` — `CHECKLISTDEK_Integration_Sync::sync()`
- `GET /integrations/{slug}/preview` → `preview_integration_sync()` — `CHECKLISTDEK_Integration_Sync::preview()`
- `POST /integrations/{slug}/push` → `push_integration()` — optional `site_ids` array; delegates to `push_agent()`
- `GET|PUT /integrations/telemetry-rules` → `get_telemetry_rules()` / `update_telemetry_rules()`

Admin AJAX handlers in `CHECKLISTDEK_Admin_Ajax` (registered on Community and Pro — same action list; admin UI prefers these over REST for integrations, site run history, and Activity Logs list on memory-constrained installs). Shared helpers: `get_request_nonce()`, `verify_ajax_nonce()`, `post_input()`, `post_bool()`; capability gates via `verify_request()` / `verify_sites_request()` / `verify_dashboard_request()`:
- `checklistdek_get_integrations` → `handle_get_integrations()` (`verify_request` / `MANAGE_SETTINGS`) — `CHECKLISTDEK_Integrations::get_statuses()`
- `checklistdek_integration_sync` → `handle_integration_sync()` — `slug` + optional `dry_run` → `CHECKLISTDEK_Integration_Sync::preview()` or `::sync()`
- `checklistdek_integration_push` → `handle_integration_push()` — optional JSON `site_ids` → `{Integration}::push_agent()`
- `checklistdek_save_wp_umbrella_token` → `handle_save_wp_umbrella_token()` — POST `token` (via `normalize_wp_umbrella_api_token()`) or `clear=1`; non-empty tokens call `CHECKLISTDEK_Integration_WP_Umbrella::verify_api_token()` before `save_wp_umbrella_api_token()`; returns `{ api_token_configured, message }` or JSON error with translatable message (401 vs 403 hints for wrong key type / missing scope)
- `checklistdek_get_telemetry_rules` → `handle_get_telemetry_rules()` — rules + field labels
- `checklistdek_save_telemetry_rules` → `handle_save_telemetry_rules()` — JSON `rules` → `CHECKLISTDEK_Integrations::save_telemetry_rules()`
- `checklistdek_get_site_runs` → `handle_get_site_runs()` (`verify_sites_request` / `MANAGE_SITES`) — `site_id`, optional `status`, `limit` (default 25, max 200), `offset` → `list_for_site_history()`
- `checklistdek_get_activity_logs` → `handle_get_activity_logs()` (`verify_dashboard_request` / `VIEW_DASHBOARD`) — filter POST fields → `CHECKLISTDEK_Audit_Log::query( list_query_args_from_input() )`

## New Integration Checklist

1. Create `includes/integrations/class-checklistdek-integration-{slug}.php` implementing `CHECKLISTDEK_Integration_Interface` (including `supports_site_sync()` and `fetch_platform_sites()` when inventory sync is supported).
2. Register in `CHECKLISTDEK_Integrations::get_all()`.
3. Add platform field mappings in `CHECKLISTDEK_Integrations::get_default_telemetry_rules()` if connector exposes sync fields.
4. Return `supports_sync`, `synced_sites`, `description`, and optional `docs_url` from `get_status()` for the connector modal.
5. When inventory sync can return zero rows, optionally implement `get_sync_diagnostics()` to return actionable hints (MainWP pattern).
6. Site sync via admin-ajax `checklistdek_integration_sync` (or REST `/integrations/{slug}/sync` and `/preview`); push agent via `checklistdek_integration_push` (or REST `/integrations/{slug}/push`); telemetry rules via `checklistdek_save_telemetry_rules` (or REST `/integrations/telemetry-rules`). When adding new integration admin actions, prefer extending `CHECKLISTDEK_Admin_Ajax` alongside REST for parity.

## Docblocks

Document public methods with `@param`, `@return`, and `@var` on class properties.
